comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T17:06:51.909Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-30: current dist reproduction confirmed role-less custom status registration succeeds silently, its item is absent from next/context, and health reports ok with zero warnings. Deliver role-required registration, SDK-owned role classification, validate/health findings, role-derived context/list aliases, contracts, docs, and sandbox acceptance."
  "2026-08-30T19:54:50.219Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-30: new custom statuses must carry an effective lifecycle role; existing definitions retain roles when omitted during updates; health/validate emit bounded legacy diagnostics; context and list aliases now use public SDK lifecycle buckets. PM-linked suite passed 6 files/212 tests. Full repository coverage passed 590/590 files and 8160/8160 tests at exactly 100% statements (60340/60340), branches (45511/45511), functions (12551/12551), and lines (58096/58096). pnpm quality:static passed including ESLint, zero duplication, architecture limits, contracts, refusal closure, token budgets, graph/record integrity, and 100% source/export/member docstrings. Trivy found 0 high/critical findings; npm audit found 0 known vulnerabilities; credential scan and ShellCheck passed. Package-first dogfood, packed npx/bunx smoke, and independent npm/npx plus Bun/bunx SDK/CLI acceptance passed, including roleless refusal and a custom active status appearing in the open lifecycle bucket."
  "2026-08-30T19:59:52.504Z","harness:codex","Final static-gate amendment: classified this shipped behavior as production_defect and recorded gate_strengthened evidence owned by pm-0mhspz. The lifecycle-role registration/selection gate names a runnable negative control plus local coverage/static/defect-evidence and hosted coverage/static/Linux/Windows checks. node scripts/release/defect-evidence-gate.mjs --json now passes all boundary, defect-evidence, and recurrence-policy checks with zero findings and no waiver."
  "2026-08-30T21:00:58.978Z","harness:codex","PR review correction evidence: accepted CodeRabbit's lifecycle findings. Context status rank, open/in-progress predicates, hierarchy, progress, workload, and sorting now derive from active_statuses and in_progress_status rather than literal ids. List tests seed built-in open/in-progress and custom active review items and assert exact result ids. Focused suite passes 81/81; full repository coverage passes 590/590 files and 8161/8161 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-30T21:02:08.791Z","harness:codex","Final correction gates: PM-linked lifecycle suite passes 6 files/212 tests and focused cross-item correction suite passes 81/81; exact repository coverage passes 590 files and 8161 tests at 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static and all security gates pass. The strengthened negative control now includes exact list-result assertions and every context lifecycle consumer."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T21:40:48.466Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduction extended 2026-07-25: the second half of this class ships inside a first-party profile, so it is reachable without anyone mis-using pm schema add-status.\n\npm profile apply research registers the custom status 'analyzing' correctly — schema/statuses.json records roles [\"active\"], pm schema show-status analyzing reports source custom, roles active, order 12, and pm profile lint research reports ok with 0 warnings. Everything the workspace is told about the status is right.\n\nAn item moved into it then behaves inconsistently across the read surface:\n  pm next            recommends it, reasons \"open and ready to start\", ready 1   (role-derived, correct)\n  pm context         active_items 1, open 0, in_progress 0                        (mixed, the arithmetic stops adding up)\n  pm list-open       count 0                                                      (literal status id, wrong)\n  pm validate        ok true, pm health ok true                                   (silent)\n\nSo list-open belongs to the literal-id half alongside context summary.open / summary.in_progress, and this item's acceptance criterion already names it in the regression-test clause. Worth keeping because it changes the severity argument: the fix is not only about guarding a mis-used flag, it is about the three shipped profiles (agile, ops, research) each adding an active-role status whose items are already invisible to list-open today. Any workspace that applies a built-in profile — the intended path for customising pm to a domain — lands in the inconsistent state without doing anything unusual."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T19:54:49.659Z","harness:codex",Customization requires semantic lifecycle roles to be a schema invariant rather than a CLI convention; role-derived SDK buckets keep every adapter consistent and let literal built-in status names remain compatibility aliases only.
